{"schemaVersion":1,"release":"20261114-evidence2","scope":"Three bounded number-state learning panels, structure-source handoff into explicit representation calculations, and an official Cu thermal-file workflow.","counts":{"oscillatorLessons":3,"oscillatorPlacements":3,"cuInputCellAtoms":4,"cuRows":251},"hooks":{"scattering-temperature":["ladder-weights"],"polaron-hamiltonian":["vacuum-motion"],"polaron-truncation":["finite-boundary"]},"verification":["Independent number-state sums and matrices check amplitudes, probabilities, separately weighted tails, microscopic reverse transitions and finite-boundary commutators against the fixed references and the existing Python API.","Course integration preserves disclosures, unfinished responses, notes and original calculator drafts; explicit copying preserves the exact chosen temperature and waits for manual calculation.","Strict source metadata preserves file/text hash identity, tolerances, basis/origin and wavevector transforms and single/double-valued selection through workbench export and explicitly saved research records. Changed requests cannot inherit unrelated source metadata.","Official Cu source bytes, lossless XZ decompression, input-cell normalization and all thermal rows are checked. Import loading, replacement, cancellation and stale completion are exercised through actual form handlers."],"boundaries":["Fixed teaching references do not introduce a general oscillator or scattering solver. Holstein vacuum and numerical truncation panels do not infer a finite-temperature polaron state.","A source checksum identifies the parsed source; it is not an electronic-structure calculation or magnetic-order detector. Imported metadata cannot independently reverify absent original bytes. Numerical representation validity and standard-label coverage remain separate.","Cu thermal_properties data describe one official calculated four-atom input cell at one volume. They do not supply eigenvectors, measured data, full quasi-harmonic volume predictions or a newly performed material calculation.","This release covers three learning hooks and representative source workflows. Broader curriculum depth, diagnosis and authentic workflows for every tool family remain open."],"files":{"GOAL-ROADMAP.md":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":50360,"sha256":"f610750dd50ca99c600b226e02c362eeafb38b4fd5459bfd744be6a2687b1d43"},"dist/app.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":97845,"sha256":"9799434a2505c13d9ab56e678b31dc26fc781255f3c9138bab5d6c23244cb0db"},"dist/bridges-ui.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":17149,"sha256":"b1c424c9e4af59e8060e36c0eb3ec138d8752774b68039932ddca364726a48ac"},"dist/data/examples/phonopy-cu-LICENSE.txt":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":1470,"sha256":"2ce26839c8b70d28765d73e934cc1a979d896d8d228d30694fdd9a92e94d43a9"},"dist/data/examples/phonopy-cu-thermal-index05.yaml":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":41975,"sha256":"1c9e6edeeded194fc7eebe9c4f4bd6e88728b48ea4f530a033240f8394267bf1"},"dist/data/examples/phonopy-cu-thermal-index05.yaml.xz":{"normalization":"raw-bytes","bytes":4900,"sha256":"36c87fc5560cc7815cd9d97105830c00cffa4a3a2fb486235d7976bc493ebb1f"},"dist/data/examples/phonopy-cu-thermal-source.json":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":2907,"sha256":"903330e565a126b3e8d30b09099ce1a352fbf0703c9d98e4cf2344e56941763f"},"dist/docs/cu-thermal-example.md":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":4040,"sha256":"69155f09dba2ab02a9a59e71a7f55b2a16ebf5bf177b295c1144eb892027a017"},"dist/index.html":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":7591,"sha256":"5f187b13884fe72e1372d64043a33d172a75f3d489c5a8557674dafa923d7eb8"},"dist/learning-bridge-host.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":4602,"sha256":"a42addc7d2d2af7074cb2a8d19a515381a68258eedfe1241b1d3eba332f0c0ba"},"dist/material-notebook.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":24768,"sha256":"5235a0176a7da2cbc7e90eae7993860059fe72eabc24100f1ec089f20b6e90e2"},"dist/material-research-ui.js":{"normalization":"utf